                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e2d69492-962f-3b07-8506-9f1d890673b3",
                        "entry_id": "2a3e8327-f989-3319-a06e-25d029f2b805",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie un ongulé, particulièrement un cervidé, qui a les os métacarpiens rapprochés du carpe et éloignés des phalanges."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "234292c2-2208-494a-86cf-1db367d05e24",
                                "sense_id": "e2d69492-962f-3b07-8506-9f1d890673b3",
                                "text": "En son temps, Brooke caractérise cette différence en disant que les Cerfs sont plésiométacarpiens et les Chevreuils télémétacarpiens (suivant que le métacarpe est rapproché ou éloigné du carpe)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ea6ae41-91b2-435c-abb8-8cf6a4153395",
                                "sense_id": "e2d69492-962f-3b07-8506-9f1d890673b3",
                                "text": "Or, tous les Cervidés de l’ancien Continent sont plésiométacarpiens, sauf les Chevreuils, et tous ceux du nouveau Continent, sauf le Wapiti, sont télémétacarpiens."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "1c7bca22-5e9b-30e9-8f65-cd4d937601ac",
                "word": "plésiométacarpien",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d8114166-d9a7-425a-a56d-d14acdc522c5",
                        "entry_id": "1c7bca22-5e9b-30e9-8f65-cd4d937601ac",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "plésiométacarpiens"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "02b1bf1b-e271-30d9-a6af-d840a174f608",
                        "entry_id": "1c7bca22-5e9b-30e9-8f65-cd4d937601ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Un cervidé qui a les os métacarpiens rapprochés du carpe et éloignés des phalanges."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9730534-fad0-46f7-8b47-9aa43f93941e",
                                "sense_id": "02b1bf1b-e271-30d9-a6af-d840a174f608",
                                "text": "On dit que le Cerf est un plésiométacarpien et le Chevreuil un télémétacarpien."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b805bba-cc95-425e-b3b2-8b80ece25f66",
                                "sense_id": "02b1bf1b-e271-30d9-a6af-d840a174f608",
                                "text": "Deux groupes de cervidés, les télémétacarpiens et les plésiométacarpiens, illustrent bien la complexité des relations entre spéciation et divergence."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "157596f7-5377-4a04-9707-e44966abf90c",
                        "source_entry_id": "1c7bca22-5e9b-30e9-8f65-cd4d937601ac",
                        "source_sense_id": "02b1bf1b-e271-30d9-a6af-d840a174f608",
                        "target_lang_word": "plesiometacarpal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "plesiometacarpal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cabaf1ca-12e8-394b-8350-e7a29354ad8d",
                                        "entry_id": "a44b675e-5262-3e34-8f5f-c689c0ffcbc4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being part of the subfamily Cervinae, having lost the parts of the second and fifth metacarpal bones closest to the foot (though retaining the parts away from the foot)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a482e0ec-6508-4254-9738-b75a04e30ae0",
                                                "sense_id": "cabaf1ca-12e8-394b-8350-e7a29354ad8d",
                                                "text": "Coordinate term: telemetacarpal"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "097d4df1-5c93-4c37-b7bf-18fc4ccdfb73",
                                                "sense_id": "cabaf1ca-12e8-394b-8350-e7a29354ad8d",
                                                "text": "However, as we emphasize elsewhere all extant plesiometacarpal (i.e., Old World) deer, of which Candiacervus is an example, give birth to one fawn per season (twins are rare to very rare)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0292ad83-8000-4183-be9f-0966b81927dd",
                                                "sense_id": "cabaf1ca-12e8-394b-8350-e7a29354ad8d",
                                                "text": "The wapiti is the only American representative of the plesiometacarpal deer, to which most Eurasian genera belong, all other American deer being telometacarpal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9de4f27b-4f37-4ef8-9659-dc3b02a9f9c5",
                                                "sense_id": "cabaf1ca-12e8-394b-8350-e7a29354ad8d",
                                                "text": "For instance, according to his views, the Virginia deer, Odocoileus, and the pampas deer, Ozotoceros, both of them telemetacarpal and having the choanae divided by the vomer, should be considered as representing subgenera of the genus Darm, the typical species of which is the European fallow deer, that is to say, a plesiometacarpal species with undivided posterior nasal aperture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
